  "bug_report_content": "Title: RandomStringUtils throws confusing IAE when end <= start\nType: Bug | Priority: Minor | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nRandomUtils invokes Random#nextInt(n) where n = end - start.\n\nIf end <= start, then Random throws:\n\njava.lang.IllegalArgumentException: n must be positive\n\nThis is confusing, and does not identify the source of the problem.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.lang3.RandomStringUtils (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.lang3.RandomStringUtils (fixed)\n@@ -241,6 +241,10 @@\n                     end = 'z' + 1;\n                     start = ' ';                \n                 }\n+            }\n+        } else {\n+            if (end <= start) {\n+                throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Parameter end (\" + end + \") must be greater than start (\" + start + \")\");\n             }\n         }"
}